<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad I Tapar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1082–<a href="/years/1118">1118</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad I Tapar was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> from 1105 to 1118, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik-Shah I</a>. After years of civil war with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berkyaruq">Berkyaruq</a> he ruled the western Seljuk lands from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, campaigning against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> and against Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. In 1108 his army defeated and killed the Mazyadid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadaqa-ibn-mansur">Sadaqa ibn Mansur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-i-tapar.jpg" alt="Muhammad I Tapar" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rashid al-Din Hamadani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Investiture_scene_of_Muhammad_I_Tapar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
